#: 0bc5f6fbdf5a449da33d8b08adb51152
msgid "The :ref:`GPS_AUTO_CONFIG<GPS_AUTO_CONFIG>` parameter provides several automatic configuration options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:145
#: 38168d5f34e9454cbd0ca46ef483d17b
msgid "0: Disable automatic configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:146
#: c23e9230c4d2491eba36434d1d8e8496
msgid "Not recommended when using supported hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:148
#: 4a886264de464537bf3257dfe0df00a0
msgid "1: Enable automatic configuration for Serial GPSes only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:149
#: 584a90f3ecce429e9a84bfe41246634d
msgid "Default value; supports many common modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:151
#: edf07f8369e44a51907a3abb0046a025
msgid "2: Enable automatic configuration for DroneCAN as well"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:152
#: 1cbc863c7d4f43e1b997c92e70b56d82
msgid "Intended for use when configuring DroneCAN GPS modules for :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw` operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:154
#: 7a97fa6734e34136baf68973b325f919
msgid "After selecting option 2 for :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw` configuration, reverting to default (non-moving-baseline) operation requires connecting to the DroneCAN peripheral(s) and manually restoring the internal GPSx_TYPE parameters to their default values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:156
#: 1fa3f2d9affd4b73a06ba2055945411d
msgid "3: Clear all configurations not set by ArduPilot (u-Blox only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:157
#: 2e2eb1ae021e45dd91f657b18dae6010
msgid "On next boot, resets u-Blox GPS modules to default before applying ArduPilot configuration values (u-Blox Generation 9 and newer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:160
#: e9b36c011f474302997da41869b1cf81
msgid "GPS Driver Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:162
#: 6c35cffdc886431eb6b1cfea394e9e49
msgid "Several GPS operating options are provided by the :ref:`GPS_DRV_OPTIONS<GPS_DRV_OPTIONS>` parameter. This parameter is a bit mask and allows multiple option selections at the same time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:164
#: 46a5a048379644a18bbfaadcac391d77
msgid "bit 0: if set, will send RTK correction data from the first GPS directly to the second via the second's UART port for :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw`, instead via the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:165
#: 604c4d6cdc5042439a489bbc270ad48b
msgid "bit 1: if set, enable SBF moving baseline yaw using custom base and GPS_MB1 offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:166
#: 37e1e61f68b7417f9485ad85cbfd8f8c
msgid "bit 2: if set, use 115.2Kbaud for max serial data rate for those GPSes not capable of higher rates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:167
#: 1e4da635f7474b6dad2c1d4d619b744d
msgid "bit 3: if set, routes RTK data between two CAN GPSes via CAN instead of via the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:168
#: f178fe5aa0014215ad941b761011a018
msgid "bit 4: if set, GPS reports altitude in ellipsoid height instead of height AMSL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:169
#: c34514612d264966ad1c79ec7a0f2c55
msgid "bit 5: if set, GPS satellite health is reported solely from L1 band (overriding L5 band health)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:170
#: 56687894714b471a852683493f045ec2
msgid "bit 6: if set, always enable RTCM decoding (even for single channel RTCM)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:171
#: 487913c7c5014b5d80d00a3343f7d434
msgid "bit 7: if set, always disable RTCM decoding (even when RTCM is seen on more than one channel)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:172
#: 41452a40829741f2aafb3569613f6b86
msgid "bit 8: if set, force u-Blox Config Get/Set (serial connected u-Blox Generation 9 and newer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:175
#: 45c9f69e46fa47458d20231710ba76ef
msgid "GPS Auto Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:177
#: 4bd45548ad5a470bb8ca64a28d67ec15
msgid "When using two GPS units there are a number of switching options that can be selected with :ref:`GPS_AUTO_SWITCH <GPS_AUTO_SWITCH>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:179
#: 9e44ec0fffb54e058d30a145104b723e
msgid "0: Use Primary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:180
#: 48d889f1b3664f61aa2d9420afaf96b4
msgid "Always use the primary GPS, this can be either the first or second as set with :ref:`GPS_PRIMARY <GPS_PRIMARY>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:182
#: 98d6a7991f434eaba52baf99f7a8b7b4
msgid "1: Use best"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:183
#: 396dd5f9bf5747aab0d51b06f50f329c
msgid "Automatically select the best GPS, this is done based on GPS fix status (2D / 3D / rtk) if both GPSs have the same fix status the one with the larger number of satellites is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:185
#: bd2ebda22fec44f69ad7888302dc20a1
msgid "2: Blend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:186
#: 2dc4329651fc40c791a087e9291ea510
msgid "Blend is best suited for use with two identical GPS units, see :ref:`GPS blending<common-gps-blending>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:188
#: f0462895a9eb4dada1bd54b695bd275a
msgid "4: Use primary if 3D fix or better"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:189
#: d1d90a647fca41898e279e9a2accfc16
msgid "Use primary GPS as set with :ref:`GPS_PRIMARY <GPS_PRIMARY>` if it has a 3D fix or better. This should be used when two dissimilar GPS units are used, one high quality primary unit, and a secondary less accurate unit. In this case the high quality GPS will often have a better quality fix even if it has fewer satellites. Using 'Use best' in this case would result in using the poorer quality GPS and result in more switching between GPS units. Unlike 'Use Primary' this option still allows falling back to the secondary GPS if 3D fix is lost on the primary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:193
#: 9b0196bbd78f4878b8357fdbde267eba
msgid "An additional variation with GPS switching is :ref:`EKF3 affinity and lane switching <common-ek3-affinity-lane-switching>`. An EKF lane can be setup to use either GPS and the whole EKF lane is then switched based on its health. If the :ref:`GPS_PRIMARY <GPS_PRIMARY>` is used for a lane, and :ref:`GPS_AUTO_SWITCH <GPS_AUTO_SWITCH>` is enabled, then the lane will use GPS info as determined by the :ref:`GPS_AUTO_SWITCH <GPS_AUTO_SWITCH>` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-positioning-landing-page.rst:196
#: f37a2e0d16114440bd12823c5ac256cd
msgid "GPS Jamming Mediation"
msgstr ""

